  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/luau-lang/luau/zipball/0.744",
  "body": "# Boo! 🦇 🎃 \r\n\r\nIn the lead up to next weeks spooky season, we've fixed a few bugs that have been lurking deep in the bowels of the runtime.\r\n\r\n## Runtime Changes\r\n- Fix a bug in DSE(Dead Store Elimination) caused by not invalidating tags when the corresponding load was overwritten\r\n- Fix an Arm64 crash caused by functions w/ more than 256 constants overflowing the arm64 immediate size.\r\n- Support Intel Mac libunwind (we just assume you're using libc++)\r\n- INVOKE_FASTPCALL should be registered as being able to invalidate SafeEnv\r\n- Fix a crash found by our fuzzer due to slot allocations.\r\n- Handful of correctness fixes to Luau integer and bit32 operations - this affects bit32.lrotate, integer.lrotate, integer.extract/replace.\r\n- Fix a bug caused by silently casting a uint8_t to an int8_t in the compiler.\r\n- Fixes a bug in FORGLOOP register reservation.\r\n\r\n## Type System Changes\r\n- Width subtyping should not inject `nil` as a type for a stand-in property. Fixes #2625, #2644.\r\n- Fix type pack handling in call tail argument position in nonstrict\r\n\r\n## Prototype/Experimental projects\r\n- Added runtime support for private class fields\r\n\r\n## New Contributors\r\n* @protheeuz made their first contribution in https://github.com/luau-lang/luau/pull/2365\r\n---\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/luau-lang/luau/compare/0.743...0.744",
